    "question": "According to De Morgan’s law, the complement of (A ∩ B) is equal to:",
    "options": {
      "A": "(A′ ∪ B′)",
      "B": "(A′ ∩ B′)",
      "C": "A ∪ B",
      "D": "A ∩ B"
    },
    "correct_answer": "A",
    "explanation": "De Morgan’s law states (A ∩ B)′ = A′ ∪ B′. The complement of an intersection becomes the union of the complements.",
    "difficulty": "Medium"
  },
